<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:Cortex">
<!--
    The control for option syscallregs on bare-metal code.  A Cortex-M RTOS
    uses `svc` for a privilege change or a context switch, and its handler
    leaves every register alone, so the compiler keeps live values in r0
    across the instruction.  FreeRTOS's MPU port raises privilege with `svc 2`
    and returns the r0 = 0 it set before it:

        8564: f3ef 8014   mrs   r0, control
              f010 0f01   tst.w r0, #1
              bf1a        itte  ne
              2000        movne r0, #0
              df02        svcne 2
              2001        moveq r0, #1
              4770        bx    lr

    (RTOSDemo.axf, xPortRaisePrivilege: returns 0 when it had to raise
    privilege and 1 when the core was already privileged.)

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow-classification.
    P0 assertion:      option syscallregs off|auto|on  (default auto).

    Pass 1 is the default `auto`, which acts only on an image the loader
    identified as a program for an operating system's user space: the svc keeps
    its old model and the function returns the r0 it set.  Pass 2 is
    `option syscallregs off`, the same.  Pass 3, `option syscallregs on`, shows
    the control is not vacuous: forced, the svc writes r0, which this handler
    does not do.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x8564" readonly="true">
eff3148010f0010f1abf002002df012070470020
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8564" name="xPortRaisePrivilege"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu xPortRaisePrivilege</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option syscallregs off</com>
  <com>lo fu xPortRaisePrivilege</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option syscallregs on</com>
  <com>lo fu xPortRaisePrivilege</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="SYSCALLREGS-CORTEXM #1: by default and with option syscallregs off the function returns a bool" min="2" max="2">bool xPortRaisePrivilege\(void\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SYSCALLREGS-CORTEXM #2: by default and with option syscallregs off it returns the r0 it set before the svc" min="2" max="2">return !v1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SYSCALLREGS-CORTEXM #3: forced on, the svc writes r0, so the default is what keeps this function right" min="1" max="1">v2 = software_interrupt\(2\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
